00:00:00.610 --> 00:00:02.220
. This is very interesting.

00:00:02.220 --> 00:00:07.240
We have the first approval rating for President
Joe Biden.

00:00:07.240 --> 00:00:09.010
It's 63 percent.

00:00:09.010 --> 00:00:17.770
This is the highest approval rating at any
time for any president dating back 12 years

00:00:17.770 --> 00:00:25.661
to 2009 to find an approval rating for a president
higher than Joe Biden's current approval rating

00:00:25.661 --> 00:00:27.590
of 63 percent.

00:00:27.590 --> 00:00:34.820
You have to go all the way back to 2009, Barack
Obama's first year in the White House when

00:00:34.820 --> 00:00:38.590
Obama hit 69 percent approval.

00:00:38.590 --> 00:00:45.150
Note that Donald Trump never got to even 50
percent approval, even one time during his

00:00:45.150 --> 00:00:46.329
entire presidency.

00:00:46.329 --> 00:00:48.950
Now, there's a couple of different things
going on here.

00:00:48.950 --> 00:00:54.720
There is such a dramatic shift in covid policy,
which is one of the top issues for most Americans

00:00:54.720 --> 00:01:00.350
right now from Trump, who couldn't have failed
more miserably to Biden, who is at least trying.

00:01:00.350 --> 00:01:02.610
And we'll see what degree of success he has.

00:01:02.610 --> 00:01:08.030
I think covid explains a lot of the shift
to a high approval rating for Joe Biden.

00:01:08.030 --> 00:01:13.299
In addition, presidents often have their best
approval ratings at the very beginning before

00:01:13.299 --> 00:01:17.910
they've done things that their political opponents
can say are bad or done, things that are actually

00:01:17.910 --> 00:01:18.910
bad.

00:01:18.910 --> 00:01:21.040
George W. Bush was different in that way.

00:01:21.040 --> 00:01:27.580
George W. Bush's approval rating skyrocketing,
I think, to eight was it 88 percent after

00:01:27.580 --> 00:01:35.159
9/11, which was not which was a bit of a ways
in Munsen to George W. Bush's presidency.

00:01:35.159 --> 00:01:39.130
But typically, this is when January, February,
March of their first term.

00:01:39.130 --> 00:01:41.150
This is when presidents have their highest
approval.

00:01:41.150 --> 00:01:44.110
So it's not totally shocking that Biden's
doing OK.

00:01:44.110 --> 00:01:46.610
Now, the fact that he's at 63 percent is quite
interesting.

00:01:46.610 --> 00:01:52.530
We've not seen an approval that high for a
president in 12 years now being realistic.

00:01:52.530 --> 00:01:56.110
Biden probably settles below 63 percent.

00:01:56.110 --> 00:02:00.909
If he can really turn the pandemic around
in the next four to six months, maybe he could

00:02:00.909 --> 00:02:03.790
get to 68, maybe he could get to 70.

00:02:03.790 --> 00:02:09.399
Remember that right now, about 30 percent
of this country is completely whack a do OK.

00:02:09.399 --> 00:02:16.099
And it's very hard for me to imagine that
Biden ceiling is much higher than 70 or 72

00:02:16.099 --> 00:02:17.780
percent anyway.

00:02:17.780 --> 00:02:25.489
So maybe a successful Biden can peak at sixty
seven, sixty eight, maybe 70, and a successful

00:02:25.489 --> 00:02:29.290
Biden would probably settle somewhere around
the mid 50s.

00:02:29.290 --> 00:02:34.569
If he does well, if he does as poorly as Trump
than you'd expect to see him in the high 30s,

00:02:34.569 --> 00:02:41.140
low 40s, the way that Donald Trump does, the
real test for Biden will be these next three

00:02:41.140 --> 00:02:42.620
to six months.

00:02:42.620 --> 00:02:43.890
What happens with the virus?

00:02:43.890 --> 00:02:49.379
What happens with vaccination when we are
up now up to a one in a quarter million vaccinations

00:02:49.379 --> 00:02:51.050
a day, which is great.

00:02:51.050 --> 00:02:55.239
And what happens when unemployment expires
for a lot of people?

00:02:55.239 --> 00:02:57.900
There are some major tests coming for Joe
Biden.

00:02:57.900 --> 00:03:01.459
But these early numbers, very, very interesting
to see.

00:03:01.459 --> 00:03:07.690
And at least to the degree that a hyper polarized
country can be united behind what a president

00:03:07.690 --> 00:03:14.990
is doing, 63 percent approval and 69 percent
approval of covid so far in this first week,

